# ⛔ A shell script with CRLF is not a shell script on Linux.
#
# `scripts/hooks/pre-push` was committed with CRLF from a Windows checkout, and
# every Linux CI leg failed with `set: Illegal option -^M` before the file
# reached its second line. Git's own core.autocrlf did not save it, so the
# requirement is stated here where it is checked rather than left to a setting
# each clone configures for itself.
#
# ⚠️ This is the SECOND place carriage returns broke this hook. The first was the
# test harness feeding CRLF on stdin, which made every comparison against the
# all-zero sha false and let four tests pass without reaching the branch they
# named. Same character, different layer.
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
